ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 35803, Oct. 1, 2025>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, from among the Presidential Decrees amended pursuant to Article 6 of the Addenda, the amendments to the Presidential Decrees which have been promulgated before this Decree enters into force but the enforcement dates of which have yet to arrive, shall enter into force on the enforcement date of the relevant Presidential Decree.
Article 2 (Repeal of other statutes or regulations)
The Decree on Organization of the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy and Its Affiliates shall be abolished.
Article 3 (Transfer of public officials following transfer of functions)
Following the transfer of affairs concerning energy (excluding affairs concerning the export of nuclear power plants and resources such as petroleum, coal, gas, and minerals), 198 public officials belonging to the previous Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy as at the time this Decree enters into force (one in political service, 6 high-ranking officials, 4 in Grade III or IV, 13 in Grade IV, 18 in Grade IV or V, 72 in Grade V, 54 in Grade VI, 19 in Grade VII, 6 in Grade VIII, and 5 in Grade IX) shall be deemed public officials belonging to the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment and thus shall be transferred from the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy to the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning public officials under jurisdiction)
Public officials belonging to the previous Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy as at the time this Decree enters into force (excluding public officials transferred to the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment pursuant to Article 3 of the Addenda) shall be deemed public officials belonging to the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Resources.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning prescribed number of public officials)
Where there is currently an excess corresponding to 8 public officials of the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy (4 Grade V public officials, 2 Grade VI public officials, one Grade VII public official, and one Grade IX public official) and 3 public officials of the affiliates thereof (2 Grade VI public officials and one Grade IX public official) reduced by the enforcement of the partially amended Decree on Organization of the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy and Its Affiliates (Presidential Decree No. 35027), the corresponding prescribed number shall be deemed to exist separately in the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Resources and institutions under its jurisdiction until such excess equals the prescribed number under that Decree.
Article 6 Omitted.

